{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.68,"content_digest":"e1a78f09e8a1c7e8cb7000e9d3429decbf6571e821ccd095bb8802177cc48160","created_at":"2026-08-22T21:55:26+00:00","direction":"principle_to_meta","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"00a5294901f6c18fdc0d70d84c799dc0c3c84e3ddc6d86499c3ca2db7015cb3f","input_tokens":5649,"latency_ms":17114,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"52a9aa9256c7bc9c47ccf42df986b3be481e6f44c729a40570fe526f11ef63d8","output_tokens":2406,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:05689048e52c7705068bac13","meta_principle_id":"meta:economics-game-theory:bounded-rationality","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:scientific-discovery:01M0NQGWPXZGN09PRAJRQQS3H3","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The principle is a task-level specialization of bounded rationality: in data-analysis search tasks, a generative AI chat interface that presents linear, summarised, and aggregated text reduces the information search, attention, and mental computation required to synthesize multiple results, thereby changing the effective decision problem for the user. This matches the meta-principle's emphasis on resource-limited decision making and interface-shaped search costs.","relation_type":"specializes","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T02:58:57+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0P5WC937PV7PKQMASBZ4D3Z"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T21:55:26+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.75,"content_digest":"cdbbc30783bc1ded1c89167a7c16d388130513eace60c4a8f66019c0e8b198a5","created_at":"2026-08-22T03:37:02+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[],"link_id":"foundation-link:0bdf5ff0fdf2f0ea2c302953","meta_principle_id":"meta:mathematics-logic:axiomatic-method","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:general:01M033NBKG9301GVN441QQE887","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The axiomatic method treats theorems as consequences of declared assumptions, so the reliability of a conclusion is conditional on the reliability of its premises. The literature claim that a conclusion cannot exceed the reliability of its least-supported premise is directly consistent with this conditional structure.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-22T04:12:58+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0KTQZ6M68SKHPKARZR7EKFP"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T03:37:02+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.72,"content_digest":"5037ac072c2f393058ade9cb8d9dd6ff9fbe8f8f6516244ea8a5d16f2c8edf43","created_at":"2026-08-22T15:10:51+00:00","direction":"principle_to_meta","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"080e12f0953203e92f0f3a578fe3313258f45ca3a9bb9e5b7fa5c1e6f5c00b5e","input_tokens":5145,"latency_ms":34388,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"0d1649fb3bcf50c892494c610bda64ae4e00c82c67919661739cd8dc30f5b2a9","output_tokens":2351,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:a752d9a2b165d623d8a8116c","meta_principle_id":"meta:engineering-optimization:human-factors","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:neuroscience-cognition:01M0N0BJCN4JG8ZQX0091S1PTF","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The collaborative-assembly finding is a concrete specialization of the human-factors meta-principle: it shows how automation transparency and operator expertise jointly shape cognitive workload in a human-robot system, consistent with the meta-principle's claim that human responses vary with expertise and that automation changes workload and monitoring demands rather than simply removing human involvement.","relation_type":"specializes","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-22T17:07:53+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0N72WTZDNS3VF5QZJB70PZ5"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"partial","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T15:10:51+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"partial","confidence":0.5,"content_digest":"c7f2c5da0aa4235e0fdc3929cafbc57e15fc20afef81231941839bdb24490885","created_at":"2026-08-23T04:40:53+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"6024648b5a20e1670e53790d19bd2378a8223f70228b4942c0583ce51ba92ee7","input_tokens":5783,"latency_ms":31249,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"1bb65d2a9c764fa2487e5764ab929836c1d656d485a41788fd98d33ea2fd6a8a","output_tokens":2483,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:a7d4e2289cbd5ff74cc6fdc4","meta_principle_id":"meta:scientific-discovery:bayesian-experimental-design","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:biology-evolution:01M0PEPW7NS9H8VDGPX1ZWCWEG","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"Selecting experiments to reduce uncertainty in an unobserved component aligns with the information-gain rationale of Bayesian experimental design. Prediction deviation may serve as a surrogate for expected information gain, but the principle does not establish that the selection rule maximizes expected information, so the relation is only consistent and requires review.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T08:08:08+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0PTK9G6V6VXNVFWAWBHMSYT"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"partial","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T04:40:53+00:00","variable_compatibility":"partial"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.75,"content_digest":"f74be4a00b2174b58473b6595bd827ae0014aa73bc855f601da7c0224ef81930","created_at":"2026-08-23T11:14:46+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"a6b05e8ebbb42f6e9c5f1c238b88b7d9a2e2c7d83216cb353e9f6282efec335a","input_tokens":6008,"latency_ms":37760,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"1afe996ff46f0ccb1d5ec02b5c0acb7bfa28584b572c317d3e122c70e70ef6be","output_tokens":2599,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:e7e07e6f0718c3c01801db37","meta_principle_id":"meta:foundations:uncertainty-propagation","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:physics:01M0Q57W84XQ7ZTNPYQ5A5N5ZX","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The claim is a variance-based sensitivity result obtained by propagating 5% uncertainties in Young's modulus and Poisson's ratio into hoop stress via surrogate models and Sobol' indices. This directly instantiates the meta-principle that output uncertainty must reflect uncertain inputs and their relative contributions. The meta-principle does not predict which input dominates, but the claim is a compatible, study-specific application of that framework.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T15:24:41+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0QKJMJD3A13DCG7YJ3ACW1G"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T11:14:46+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
